/**
 * Every SRD 5.1 spell, cantrips through 9th level.
 *
 * This work includes material taken from the System Reference Document 5.1 ("SRD 5.1") by
 * Wizards of the Coast LLC, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (see docs/NOTICE.md). Cantrip and 1st-level
 * descriptions are condensed paraphrases; higher levels are condensed from the SRD text.
 *
 * kind:
 *   'attack'  — spell attack roll (attackType 'ranged' | 'melee'), damage on hit
 *   'save'    — target saves (save ability) vs your spell DC; onSave 'half' | 'none'
 *   'auto'    — always hits (Magic Missile)
 *   'heal'    — restores HP (+ spellcasting modifier)
 *   'temp_hp' — grants temporary HP
 *   'utility' — narrative effect; some set an engine-tracked effect (see `effect`)
 * scales: cantrip damage dice grow at character levels 5, 11 and 17.
 * upcast: dice added per slot level above the spell's level (damage, or healing for 'heal').
 * area: a save spell that hits every engaged enemy (one damage roll, a separate open save each).
 * healMod: false when a healing spell does not add your spellcasting modifier.
 */

